00:26:26.970 --> 00:26:29.040
where their culture was denigrated,

550
00:26:29.040 --> 00:26:31.920
where they just found thousands of bodies

551
00:26:31.920 --> 00:26:33.780
of these children in Canada,

552
00:26:33.780 --> 00:26:36.000
who died in these residential schools.

553
00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:40.050
Now, those that survived the residential schools

554
00:26:40.050 --> 00:26:41.310
and went home,

555
00:26:41.310 --> 00:26:43.713
their whole childhood had been robbed from them.

556
00:26:44.760 --> 00:26:46.920
Their parenting was taken away.

557
00:26:46.920 --> 00:26:49.890
Their nurturing connections were destroyed.

558
00:26:49.890 --> 00:26:52.350
They didn't know how to parent the next generation.

559
00:26:52.350 --> 00:26:54.450
And this went on for 100 years.

560
00:26:54.450 --> 00:26:56.520
So, in the Native communities in Canada,

561
00:26:56.520 --> 00:26:59.433
we have much more alcoholism, much more child abuse.

562
00:27:00.450 --> 00:27:03.090
This is contrary how they used to raise children.

563
00:27:03.090 --> 00:27:05.490
These indigenous people raise children

564
00:27:05.490 --> 00:27:07.470
in much more healthier ways than we do.

565
00:27:07.470 --> 00:27:08.880
Right, right.

566
00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:11.703
I mean, we need to learn for how they raise children.

