00:28:49.170 --> 00:28:53.100
And where we're out of balance

602
00:28:53.100 --> 00:28:57.090
is that we have certain needs as human beings.

603
00:28:57.090 --> 00:28:58.890
See, children have four basic needs.

604
00:28:59.937 --> 00:29:02.997
The need to be strongly attached to adults

605
00:29:02.997 --> 00:29:04.923
who take care of them,

606
00:29:04.923 --> 00:29:06.930
and who are with them all the time, by the way,

607
00:29:06.930 --> 00:29:10.440
'cause as we evolved as human beings over millions of years,

608
00:29:10.440 --> 00:29:14.790
and for most of our species, existence as homo sapiens.

609
00:29:14.790 --> 00:29:16.890
We lived in small communities

610
00:29:16.890 --> 00:29:19.080
where the parents were always around the kids.

611
00:29:19.080 --> 00:29:21.240
So, secure attachments.

612
00:29:21.240 --> 00:29:22.470
And extended family.

613
00:29:22.470 --> 00:29:24.750
Extended family, well, community, right?

614
00:29:24.750 --> 00:29:28.650
And then children have a need not to have to work

615
00:29:28.650 --> 00:29:31.110
to make their relationship with the parents work.

616
00:29:31.110 --> 00:29:34.140
They have to be able to rest in a security,

617
00:29:34.140 --> 00:29:35.790
that there's nothing they can do

618
00:29:35.790 --> 00:29:37.380
to destroy their relationship,

619
00:29:37.380 --> 00:29:39.603
and there's nothing they need to do to make it work.

620
00:29:39.603 --> 00:29:43.680
That in our society, we make our kids work to be accepted.

621
00:29:43.680 --> 00:29:45.960
You have to be good, you have to be smart,

622
00:29:45.960 --> 00:29:47.850
you have to be good-looking

623
00:29:47.850 --> 00:29:51.480
or you have to be behave acceptably,

624
00:29:51.480 --> 00:29:53.220
otherwise you're gonna get a timeout.

625
00:29:53.220 --> 00:29:56.640
And we're gonna say to you, "No, you can't be with us.

626
00:29:56.640 --> 00:29:59.697
We're gonna deprive you of our contact for a little while."

627
00:30:00.720 --> 00:30:03.330
Jordan Peterson, a Canadian psychologist,

628
00:30:03.330 --> 00:30:06.660
says that an angry child should be made to sit by themselves

629
00:30:06.660 --> 00:30:08.220
until they come back to normal.

630
00:30:08.220 --> 00:30:10.740
In other words, it's not normal for a kid to be angry.

631
00:30:10.740 --> 00:30:11.573
Well, let me tell you,

632
00:30:11.573 --> 00:30:13.680
it's very normal for a two-year-old to be angry

633
00:30:13.680 --> 00:30:14.820
'cause they get frustrated.

634
00:30:14.820 --> 00:30:16.717
Now, if you give the message to a two-year-old,

635
00:30:16.717 --> 00:30:18.660
"You're not acceptable to me when you're angry."

636
00:30:18.660 --> 00:30:20.940
Basically you're saying to them, "Don't be yourself.

637
00:30:20.940 --> 00:30:23.677
Suppress who you are in order to be accepted."

638
00:30:23.677 --> 00:30:25.140
"Love is conditional."

639
00:30:25.140 --> 00:30:27.030
Love is conditional, that's the message you're giving.

640
00:30:27.030 --> 00:30:28.680
A lot of kids in this society

641
00:30:28.680 --> 00:30:30.630
are getting the message that love is conditional.

642
00:30:30.630 --> 00:30:35.463
We tell parents not to pick up their crying babies.

643
00:30:36.480 --> 00:30:37.313
We tell them that--

644
00:30:37.313 --> 00:30:40.470
Right, that they need to learn how to be okay

645
00:30:40.470 --> 00:30:41.640
without that nurturing.

646
00:30:41.640 --> 00:30:42.840
That's so crucial in that--

647
00:30:42.840 --> 00:30:45.630
You tell a mother gorilla not to pick up their baby

648
00:30:45.630 --> 00:30:46.920
when it's crying.

649
00:30:46.920 --> 00:30:50.703
We tell a mother cat to ignore the little kid's miaowing.

650
00:30:54.450 --> 00:30:58.680
So that children have the need to be able to experience

651
00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:00.363
all their emotions fully.

